{
  "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
  "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Allon Kedem, Esq., on behalf of Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kedem: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: As its name suggests, the Armed Career Criminal Act singles out the most intractable offenders for the harshest punishments by requiring three qualifying offenses \"committed on occasions different from one another.\" That phrase does not apply to defendants like Mr. Wooden, who commit their crimes in a single criminal episode."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You seem to define the occasion as a distinct criminal opportunity. How would you -- how are we to analyze that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: No, I understand that, but I think you were saying a few minutes ago that it matters whether the offenses -- the example of the crime boss, it matters whether the offenses are different --whether they are separate -- different offenses or whether it's three offenses of the same kind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "because the Solicitor General in that case pointed to state cases that rejected enhancements in situations no different from this one, including the Tavares case, which involved two burglaries on the same day."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KEDem",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: So \"episode\" is related activities or events that are separated from others by a discontinuity or clean break."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Ms. Ross, is there any way using either your test or Petitioner's test to avoid fact-finding that seems to run the risk of involving us with the Sixth Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you know this? How do you know this? I mean, what we have is a piece of paper 15 years old or 10 years old, and it says on it pled guilty, charge, robbery."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under what understanding of \"episode\" or \"occasion\" would a common person walk away and say, nope, those were different occasions, and so, yes, even though that person has only had one episode, one evening of burglary, he's now a career offender?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, no. No, no, no. If we think that there's ambiguity either way, okay, if we think that there's going to be confusion either way, then what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Ross, I have one question. If we conclude that someone who goes down the street and burglarizes different houses and different cars going down the street, that that's all one occasion, if that's our common-sense intuition to borrow your phrase, you would disagree with that, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the confrontation clause question, again, if we do disagree with you and we think that -- that \"occasion\" is -- is broader than you suggest, does that raise Sixth Amendment concerns?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allon Kedem (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b09e2d807fbad0c108b4002a7cecc98f94a0fd17ecf7e38c52d5bd8381b2f90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b09e2d807fb-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question -- a -- a test described as an essential elements test raises for me a number of questions. First of all, are there elements of an offense which are not essential? For instance, mens rea?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-5279",
